  "revision_note": "v1 (c3320ed) registered the AT1 module, its acceptance suite, the design/report and the matrices.  v2 refreshes them because the user ruling for B3-AT2A required a TERMINOLOGY CORRECTION inside AT1: the default publish mode was renamed from `atomic` to `staged_then_single_pass` (the old string is kept only as a deprecated alias), the publish-state vocabulary STAGED_VALIDATED / PUBLISHING / COMMITTED / COMMITTED_VERIFIED / PARTIAL_COMMIT / OUTCOME_UNKNOWN was added and recorded per publish, and AT1 now reports explicitly committed_verified=false because it performs no independent post-commit re-read.  B3AT1_DESIGN.md and B3AT1_REPORT.md gained errata sections instead of having their conclusions rewritten.  The AT1 suite was re-run after the change and all 13 verdicts are unchanged; the per-instance evidence was refreshed.  No pin changed and v1 stays byte-intact."
